            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="VIZ01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William</forename>
                        <surname>Vizard</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1774">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1859"/>
                    <occupation>Lawyer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Probably William Vizard (DNB 1774-1859). A young lawyer who subsequently worked with
                            Brougham and later as Queen Caroline's attorney. </p> <p> Pope suggests: 'Godwin was perhaps
                            asking him for financial help and may have taken him to Joseph Johnson's
                            to get the latter's security. Godwin then called on Vizard when Johnson
                            was ill, two days before he died, and Vizard came to the funeral and
                            then called on Godwin the next day.' </p> <p> It is certainly true that most contacts are calls on Vizard by Godwin.</p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
